      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmmm... SkString is already 8 bytes, it\u0027s really an `sk_sp\u003cSkString::Rec\u003e`. I suppose this could potentially save a ref and unref (which are basically never contended). Earlier there was a version of this which could return a new empty SkString which couldn\u0027t be returned by reference, but now that isn\u0027t happening due to fixing the struct type logic and asserting that there is an active structure element instead.\n\nThat being said, there is just one caller which requires a value and it will just be moved multiple times down into the union, it will be emitted, and then destructed. This would need to happen anyway, so it doesn\u0027t currently change anything.",
